{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"APPROVED RP-04 decision: the initial public Python seam accepts provider-native credential, identity, or session capabilities into Rebar-owned factories. It does not accept arbitrary fully constructed SDK clients or runners that could bypass Rebar retry, timeout, cache, output, error, or lifecycle policy. Examples are boto3 Session, Anthropic AccessTokenProvider, OpenAI workload identity/callable key provider, and provider-specific static adapter input. Rebar constructs, owns, and closes the official SDK client that PydanticAI receives. A future provider that only supports whole-client injection requires a separate evidence-backed design exception. Also recorded the next unapproved carrier question: Pydantic SecretStr/SecretBytes mask repr/str/default JSON and require explicit unwrap, but do not protect memory and hash from the underlying value; the candidate use is only in provider-specific non-serializable static-auth containers with comparison/hash exclusion and existing canary leakage tests. Rebar currently has no SecretStr/SecretBytes usage. Gitleaks found no leaks."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786937334902505001,"uuid":"88ef9d20-931a-4180-9316-80c8354281c1"}